-- functions.spl — LLM function definitions for Recipe 97: PDF Digest via RAG
--
-- One function: digest_section_writer — answers a single digest question
-- using only the retrieved context chunks, with no knowledge of the full
-- document structure.  Called once per schema question; results are assembled
-- by assemble_rag_digest in tools.spl.

CREATE FUNCTION digest_section_writer(question TEXT, context TEXT, max_tokens INT)
RETURNS TEXT
AS $$
You are a research analyst answering ONE specific question about a document.
You will be given the question and the most relevant excerpts from the document,
retrieved by semantic search. Answer using ONLY the information in these excerpts
— do not invent details not present in them. If the excerpts do not contain
enough information to answer fully, say what you can and note the gap.

Question: {question}

Relevant excerpts:
{context}

Write a clear, factual answer in plain prose. Stay well under {max_tokens} words
— generation is cut off at a hard token limit with no warning. For the
contributions question, use exactly 3 bullet points. For all other questions,
write 2-4 complete sentences and stop. No preamble like "Based on the excerpts..."
$$;
